ous we have a  photograph of  the members of the excavation crew  serving as lincoln's pallbearers  bringing the coffin into the tomb and so  in ceremonies that they hadn't even  taken their hats off while they were  doing it  then there was one other final witness  who was going to come one of the members  of the lincoln guard was a man named  joseph lindley and he had a 13 year old  son named fleetwood fleetwood was in  school that day and that morning a note  arrived in fleetwood's classroom for his  teacher  and it was a note please excuse  fleetwood and tell him to hop on his  bicycle and pedal over to the oak ridge  as fast as he can and with all the  enthusiasm of any 13 year old boy who's  been led out of school early  fleetwood was on the bicycle and heading  to the cemetery like a shot  came so fast that he actually left off  his bicycle at the tomb door and rolled  the bicycle into memorial hall  and inside was his father and all these  other witnesses and the coffin of  abraham lincoln on two wooden saw horses  and the kid realized what he was about  to see because there were two other  individuals in the memorial hall that  day there were two springfield plumbers  leon hopkins and his brother-in-law  charles willey they were there to cut  the lead sheath  there was going to be a final  identification of the remains of abraham  lincoln robert lincoln had not  authorized this the lincoln guard had  taken it upon themselves to do this  and the plumbers cut through the sheath  and they raised the lid and everybody  crowded around and there was abraham  lincoln perfectly preserved  the wart on the cheek the tuft of beard  on the chin the unruly black hair  and  fleetwood said later that he wasn't  frightened at the time but for the next  six months he had lincoln nightmares  and now that the now that the  identification had been completed they  closed the lid resealed the coffin um by  the way just a little tangential thing  leon hopkins the plumber had been